On Tue, Nov 27, 2012 at 4:52 PM, zhouzaiwei <zhouz...@163.com> wrote:
>
>
>  Great!
> By your code it works well and never show errors.

Good.  Then you start increasing the RAM setting to see if you can use
more than RAM=0.1.  I'm sure can increase.

> at the begain of start R, I use code ">memory.limit()" it shows "
> 1535",and ">memory.limit(T)" shows "14",
> Does that mean i have not load previous data?

Don't really know.  I never use those memory.*() functions, so don't
know how to interpret it.

>From the aroma point of view, the aroma framework only keeps any data
in memory when it's really needed.

> I have 8G RAM but the 32 bit
> windows xp OS only recognize 3.25GB.

Yupp.  But even 3.25GB is plenty for aroma.  So, I'm quite sure you
ran out of memory because you had old objects sitting around.

> I used to set RAM by code:setOption(aromaSettings, "memory/ram", 0.1) , it
> seems the function is not like setRam(aromaSettings, 0.1) ,what is the
> difference between them?

You're correct to assume that those two calls should be equivalent.
...and they should be.  However, there was a bug in the version you
used causing only setRam() to work, which is why I told you to use
that one.  If you install the latest version:

source("http://aroma-project.org/hbLite.R");
hbInstall("aroma.affymetrix");

you should also get aroma.core v2.7.1 [see
packageVersion("aroma.core")] and then both approaches work.

/Henrik

